  "body_markdown": "This brief distinguishes source reporting from SecOpsAI's original observations.\n\n## CVE-2026-119977: WordPress Core Time-of-check Time-of-use (TOCTOU) Race Condition Vulnerability\n\nSource-reported by [CISA Known Exploited Vulnerabilities](https://www.cisa.gov/sites/default/files/feeds/known_exploited_vulnerabilities.json).\n\nCISA Known Exploited Vulnerabilities reports: CVE-2026-119977: WordPress Core Time-of-check Time-of-use (TOCTOU) Race Condition Vulnerability. CVE-2026-119977 (official CVSS 8.1): WordPress Core is vulnerable to Remote Code Execution in versions 4.7 through 7.1.3. CISA lists it as exploited in the wild.\n\nDefensive action: Apply mitigations in accordance with vendor instructions, ensuring compliance with CISA\u2019s BOD 26-04 Prioritizing Security Updates Based on Risk guidance and CISA\u2019s \u201cForensics Triage Requirements\u201d. Follow applicable BOD 26-04 guidance for cloud services or discontinue use of the product if mitigations are unavailable. Stakeholders are responsible for evaluating each asset's internet exposure and ensuring adherence to BOD 26-04 patching guidelines.\n\nLimitations: Source-reported; SecOpsAI did not reproduce the issue.\n\nPublished: not supplied; first observed: 2026-11-03T22:56:36.022450Z.\n\nVerified automatically by SecOpsAI rules (identifiers and scores checked against cve.org and NVD) under the editor's recorded policy.\n\n| Claim | Check | Source |\n\n| --- | --- | --- |\n\n| CVE-2026-119977 exists | confirmed | https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-119977 |\n\n| CVSS 8.1 | confirmed | https://services.nvd.nist.gov/rest/json/cves/2.0?cveId=CVE-2026-119977 |\n\n| exploited in the wild | confirmed | https://www.cisa.gov/known-exploited-vulnerabilities-catalog |\n\nSecOpsAI detection: no SecOpsAI rule covers this yet.\n\n## Stanza: RCE via pickle deserialization in the lemmatizer\n\nSource-reported by [GitHub Security Advisories](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-gh9r-c94j-cmp5).\n\nGitHub Security Advisories reports: Stanza: RCE via pickle deserialization in the lemmatizer. CVE-2026-115878 (official CVSS 7.8): Stanza is a Stanford NLP Python library for tokenization, sentence segmentation, NER, and parsing of many human languages. The source also mentions CVE-2026-54499.\n\nDefensive action: Upgrade to a fixed release: stanza 1.15.0.\n\nLimitations: Source-reported; SecOpsAI did not reproduce the issue.\n\nPublished: 2026-11-03T20:29:16Z; first observed: 2026-11-03T21:15:35.601280Z.\n\nVerified automatically by SecOpsAI rules (identifiers and scores checked against cve.org and NVD) under the editor's recorded policy.\n\n| Claim | Check | Source |\n\n| --- | --- | --- |\n\n| CVE-2026-115878 exists | confirmed | https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-115878 |\n\nSecOpsAI detection: no SecOpsAI rule covers this yet.\n\nSecOpsAI deployment exposure: PyPI / Python.\n\n## Collection scope\n\nCollection is bounded and does not establish comprehensive surveillance. 0 enabled sources lack a fresh successful collection. 5 registry collectors provide metadata coverage without artifact scanning. Unknown eligible-event and evidence-coverage denominators are reported as unknown.\n\n## Credits and corrections\n\nPrepared by Onyedika Christopher Agada. Technical verification and final release require recorded human review. Corrections will retain the previous edition and explain material changes.",
